# IDN Site Manager's settings (read by its service at start):
#   sudo systemctl restart idn-site-manager   after a change.
#
# The panel's site password (at least 6 characters), set at each start. Or leave it out
# and set it on the console's panel-password command, once.
#IDN_SITE_PASSWORD=
#
# Devices that know this join without approval (and can still be revoked).
#IDN_PASSPHRASE=
#
# More options (idn-site-manager --help), e.g. off the site's own network (a VPS):
#   --no-announce        don't announce the site on mDNS (IDN Nodes are given its address)
#   --panel-port 29202    the web panel's port (https)
#   --port 5959          the discovery server's port
#IDN_SITE_MANAGER_ARGS=
#
# A computer with IDN Media runs its Site Manager inside the IDN Node instead
# (idn-node set sitemanager-on=true): not both on one machine (the same ports).
